WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.900
Work together with your comrades and attain victory!

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.900
Prowl this vast battlefield and crush the opposition!

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.170
This is the 24-hour tournament.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.780
Applications are open!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:15.820
Fight, and keep fighting!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:15.820
Taking
Applications!

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.810
Come again.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.170
An illegal weapon mod?

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.910
Yeah, the gun's beefed up with high pressure gas.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.620
They arrested the one who did the mod,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.500
but he sold one gun before they got to him.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.740
Did they catch the one who bought it?

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:45.480
Nope.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.670
Nobody knows who has it.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:53.030
The clerk told me to go to the police
if I had any tips that could help them.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.000
Well, only nice people play airsoft.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.580
You're way too serious, Yura.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.560
But man, this is some awful timing.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.870
The 24-hour tournament is soon.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.020
I hope we can all steer clear of trouble.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.550
Me too.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.130
I'm really excited for this tournament, too!

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.640
I even bought an extended magazine for Choujirou!

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.060
We could try gunning for the grand prize with that enthusiasm.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:22.920
I hope so.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.720
I will...

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.640
Come on, relax.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.520
These tournaments don't come often, so try to enjoy it.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:34.600
That's exactly why I want to win it.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.950
Rin and her team will be there too, you know?

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.200
This time I won't let her...

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.200
Yura!

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.580
A BB pellet?

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:52.980
Are we under fire?

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.000
Is someone...

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.070
shooting at us?

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:12.070
STELLA GIRLS' ACADEMY

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:12.070
HIGH SCHOOL DIVISION C  CLUB

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:15.570
I decided this myself

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.570
I decided that relying on chance

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:24.080
is just so ridiculously fruitless

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:29.040
I dwelled in my fantasies too much

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.960
I'm going to leave my safety zone behind

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.880
I try to keep my future in my crosshairs,

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:44.180
and even though my aim is unsteady,

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.520
I will hold my head high

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.190
I'll change my life,

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.230
and the gray rules that govern it

00:02:54.230 --> 00:03:00.070
even if I trip and stumble on the way

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:05.990
Others are guiding me, but I will walk

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:12.710
My footprints in this world are so colorful

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.190
Five o'clock, second floor.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:37.440
An assassin's bullet hath slain my comrade.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.330
That's the shooter.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.440
This is pretty dangerous. Look.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.900
That gun punched a hole in the steel can, so it has to be modded.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.420
One hit'll do more than just sting.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.830
We should try to escape.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:45.540
No.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.950
I'll catch the shooter.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.480
Yura, that's dangerous!

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.950
I can't let someone get away with this!

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.510
Airguns aren't meant for evil!

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.220
Okay, listen...

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.190
That was close.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.070
I'm sorry, Sono.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:23.840
Call an ambulance!

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:24.920
Are you okay?

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.580
Sono?

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:26.280
Hey!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.370
What's wrong?

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.770
Hey, Sono.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.410
How ya feelin'?

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.270
Hey, thanks for coming.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:00.390
Sorry about the trouble.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:04.160
W-We're not troubled.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.570
Aren't you hurt pretty bad?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.660
Dodging the car and rolling on
concrete wasn't the issue.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.510
I just didn't land well.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.080
You must be in pain.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.040
They say I've got a light concussion,

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.970
but the real problem is my sprained ankle.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:20.000
I can't do airsoft for three weeks.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.880
Three weeks?

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.430
But the 24-hour tournament...

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.600
Well, nothing we can do about it.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.550
Damn it!

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.170
Man, when I get my hands on that shooter...

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:35.420
Just let the cops handle it.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.610
Focus on the tournament.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:41.070
Try to have fun there in my stead.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.380
That's what's most important.

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:47.150
Well, I guess...

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.220
It's my fault.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:00.030
She tried to rescue me...

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.190
Let me...

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.710
Let me quit the C3 club in apology!

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.990
Calm down, Yura.

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:12.250
What good is it going to do if you quit?

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.640
And besides, it's the shooter's fault!

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:16.840
Yeah!

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.350
Sono tried to calm me down, but I just can't stomach this!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:24.660
But why would someone try to shoot Sono?

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:28.190
Maybe it's out of hatred?

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:30.840
Goodness!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.740
Haruna Rin!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.860
H-Hold on.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:38.470
That's a pretty big accusation.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.530
It's a crime.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.820
But she's totally the type to do it, isn't she?

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:44.800
Right, Yura?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.290
I...

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.930
I don't think...

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:55.560
people who do airsoft are evil enough to do that...

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.080
I-I guess...

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.140
Maybe I got carried away.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.830
She's never done something like this.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:04.330
Yeah.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:09.620
The real question is what we'll do about the 24-hour tournament.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.200
It'll be hard without Sono.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.250
There'll be a ton of veteran teams from all over the country.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:18.320
We'll never win with our current skill.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:22.040
I don't think it'd be fun for me without Sono.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.040
Yeah...

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.420
We should just drop out.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:37.760
Sorry.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:42.300
I forgot something in Sono's room.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.930
Go without me.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:53.990
I'm coming in.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:56.020
Sono...

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:04.170
She fell asleep.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.300
I want to talk about the tournament.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:14.030
The others want to stay home because you won't be there.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:19.260
What should I do here?

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.560
That's not...

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.060
That's not the C3 club I've come to know!

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.820
I'm sorry.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.720
I'll take care of it.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.690
I'll fill in for you.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:38.200
So don't worry. Just get some rest.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.840
High School Division   Twelfth Grade   Kashima Sonora

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.840
High School Division    Tenth Grade      Yamato Yura

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:50.390
<i>Yes...</i>

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.090
<i>I should be able to do it too.</i>

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.090
Hey, you got any plans for the holidays?

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.800
I'm going overseas!

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.210
My parents and I are doing some traveling, too.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:01.600
Sounds lovely.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.980
What'cha wanna do over the summer?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:11.740
I guess we never applied for the 24-hour tournament.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.370
Wouldn't've won anyway.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.840
By the way, where's Li'l Yura?

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:22.560
Haven't seen her around the club room much.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.620
I think she's been studying a lot.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.130
She's even reading something walking around.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:31.740
I wonder if her final marks were bad.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:34.560
Maybe I should enroll for some classes over the summer too.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.800
Since there won't be a tournament and all.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:51.320
I signed us up for the 24-hour tournament.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:56.510
I thought you were studying!

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:57.480
Nope.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:59.320
I compiled these!

00:09:59.320 --> 00:09:59.370
Classified

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:03.520
The C3 club's surefire strategy?

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:04.240
Yup!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.910
Tactical procedures for woodlands, part A.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:11.060
This is tactical information, right?

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.250
Lemme see.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:16.420
Wow, there are a lot of scenarios here.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:20.590
Urban warfare, frontal assaults, defenses.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:26.870
Helicopter drops, amphibious assaults, anti-tank warfare, anti-air warfare...

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:30.020
These last ones have nothing to do with airsoft!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:37.070
I took our fighting styles into consideration to draft guidelines for any scenarios I could think of.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:38.740
Hold on...

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.350
This looks fun!

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.550
You're amazing, Yura!

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:50.290
We always let Hono come up with a plan right before the battle started.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.410
That's true.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:54.640
Some of this is pretty far-fetched, but much of it is probably useful.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:57.130
If we pull this off, we might stand a chance!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:00.130
I say we let Yura try being the leader.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.120
Agreed!

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.970
It's kind of weird without Sono around, though.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.660
Let's do this!

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:12.350
Let's all work together so we can win the 24-hour tournament!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.020
For Sono!

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.710
Fine...

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:30.890
The 24-hour tournament comes down to the struggle for a limited number of neutral flags.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:35.590
Since we lack members, it's unrealistic to think that we'll find the flags first.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:40.940
As such, we should plan around stealing the flags of other teams.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:42.920
This is where Yura comes in.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:47.250
We'll split into attackers and defenders.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:51.810
Kari will be the main attacker, with Ren backing her up.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.880
Those two will work together to steal enemy flags

00:11:55.880 --> 00:12:00.820
while the rest of us will try to hinder and divide the enemy teams.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:06.740
This strategy hinges on our ability to respond swiftly and efficiently to enemy contact.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.830
We need to act in unison.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.290
Let's do this, girls!

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:12.750
10 days  until
the tournament

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:14.750
Let's go!

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:21.840
Sorry!

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.900
You jumped out of that bush too early, Kari!

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.760
Work together with Ren!

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:32.810
Don't start running simultaneously!

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:43.000
You're not working together at all!

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:49.190
Kari always runs behind enemy lines, and Hono and Hachiyo always act out of sync.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:50.700
Ren isn't paying attention enough.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:54.710
You're all talented individuals, but it's meaningless if you can't work as a team!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:58.840
You also spend way too much time deciding your formations.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:04.710
I want you to deploy in under thirty seconds!

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.990
Easier said than done!

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:09.240
That's gonna take forever to sink in.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:10.810
Make it happen!

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.810
Everyone has to move in unison!

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:17.060
Just like Rin's team did!

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:21.100
Otherwise, we won't stand a chance against her.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:22.860
Do you want to win or not?!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:31.240
Man, do you really want to go this far just to win?

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:37.440
I really thought Yura'd be more chill than this.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.880
I'm sure she's just doing everything she can.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.270
I bet she feels really guilty.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:45.140
She probably thinks Sono is missing because of her.

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:50.420
Seriously, though, this is too stressful.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:52.090
Honestly.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:02.290
<i>I'm sure they'll understand.</i>

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:05.440
They will once we win!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:03.210
We'll give you the trophy once they let you out!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:03.210
C3 Club Members

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:03.290
We'll give you the trophy once they let you out!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:03.290
C3 Club Members

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:03.290
Pew Pew

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:26.090
Finally, the time has come!

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:28.450
Welcome to our airsoft festival!

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:32.200
The fifth 24-hour tournament is about to begin!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:39.960
57 teams will battle each other in an area five times that of the Tokyo Dome.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.240
Please don't fire your guns outside the skirm grounds!

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:53.180
So this is the 24-hour tournament!

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:54.910
What is it?

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:55.810
Nothing.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:58.650
I just thought you were back to your old self.

00:15:58.650 --> 00:15:59.680
Yeah.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.640
I like you best this way.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:05.440
Aren't you kind of impressed with the crowds, too?

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:08.580
Yeah, it's the biggest airsoft festival out there.

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.900
There are a ton of food stalls and shops too.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:15.530
Gunsmiths, companies displaying their
ewest products, everything...

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.790
They're selling M16 airguns there!

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:23.880
There's a fanfic corner too.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.640
The loot's mine!

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:26.480
Let's go!

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:27.460
Hold on!

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.020
Don't you want to buy something too, Yura?

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:32.110
This only comes once a year.

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:35.090
I'm fine.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.590
Come on, Ren!

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:45.850
And we're back!

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:48.130
We bought a ton!

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:50.320
You're taking this too easy!

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:51.790
We have a match later.

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:53.440
Oh, relax.

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:55.100
It's a festival, remember?

00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:56.740
We can't let it go to waste.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.170
But...

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:01.390
I can't enjoy it without Sono!

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:02.700
Are you serious?

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.680
Calm down, both of you.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:06.250
Hey there, Stella girls.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:12.410
You were from Seikou Academy, right?

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.260
They're The O.C.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:17.420
Finally got your ragtag squad assembled?

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.350
And what do you need those huge suitcases for?

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:23.290
We had to come suitably equipped for our big moment.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.840
Oh, you two haven't met each other, right?

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:27.490
This guy is Tsubaki Hibiki.

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:29.310
He's our sniper.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.510
I'm Mochizuki Miyagi.

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:34.440
I'm going to enroll at Stella's next year!

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.650
So very nice...

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:39.160
to meet you.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.160
Hey, don't do that.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.660
I'm sorry, my little sister can be like that.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.500
She's a big fan of Sonora.

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:50.500
I'm her brother, Mochizuki Yoichi.

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:54.900
You're that big talent who won against Sonora, right?

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.560
I've heard the story.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:58.590
It was just water guns.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.980
Speaking of Sonora.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:04.520
Will she be okay?

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.070
Aw, don't worry about her.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:09.100
Let us perform as we always have.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:13.840
But this tournament will be quite difficult for you without Sonora, your ace.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.780
Even if you ignore Meisei,

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.610
there's Team Grizzly from Hokkaido.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:23.080
And Team Cop over there was formed around some employers at a gun manufacturer.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:29.080
To live up to their name, they all use handguns and wear police uniforms.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.820
They're supposed to be pretty good, though.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.930
They make the guns, I guess.

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:37.870
Those guys look cool!

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:42.440
Those foreigners are all active duty marines.

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:44.640
They're one of the best contenders.

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:49.140
Speaking of which, so are your pals over there.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:54.030
Spearheaded by Aoi, the Seto Family said they'd be representing Kansai here.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:58.470
Rumor has it they want to get back at you.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:00.990
Let 'em come.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.700
You know a lot about all these people.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.290
We're...

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:06.990
Seikou's intelligence agency!

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:07.950
Seikou's intelligence agency!

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:08.960
Seikou's intelligence agency!

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:13.670
The PRISM of the opera!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.260
We know all your strengths and weaknesses too.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:22.390
Let's give it all we can.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.850
Aye. Wouldn't have it any other way.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.090
Let's get started too.

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:35.100
We have to sort out some formalities first.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:39.150
I'll go take care of our luggage.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.240
I'll help you!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:45.070
All participants, please register here!

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:48.240
Once you've done so, please pick up your provisions!

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.990
What kind of provisions?

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:52.370
Food, drink, BB pellets,

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:58.480
and starting this year, a PDA for each team too to stay in touch with each other.

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:01.380
They sure lavish us with goodies.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.670
Haruna Rin!

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.360
I was told that Sonora would be in the hospital for a while.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:21.550
How strange for her to be injured where she was.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.900
Say what?

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.240
Where she was?

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.490
Sounds to me like you were there.

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:30.510
I happened to walk by.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:34.750
I had no idea I'd see Sono reduced to such a state, though.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.220
Reduced to what?

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:39.630
You were just walking by, huh?

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:41.690
What else could I have been doing?

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:43.010
Hey, Karira.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.400
Who knows?

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:49.010
It sure is pretty convenient for you that she's out of action.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:53.140
I would crush you with or without her.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.520
I'll do whatever it takes.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.020
<i>Whatever it takes?</i>

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.410
Amuse me later, okay?

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:02.830
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:03.350
Karira!

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:05.030
Weren't you and Sono friends way back?

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:11.410
That's precisely the reason why I can't forgive her.

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:17.000
I really think it was her who shot Sono.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.200
That's a dangerous accusation!

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:21.670
It might have been a coincidence, just like she said.

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:24.550
She really was there, huh?

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.760
Anyway, she's definitely gonna eat pellet!

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.220
Meisei is a strong team.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:34.430
I know!

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:37.080
But we've practiced so much!

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.360
Right?

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:39.440
Hey!

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:41.940
We put our luggage in the lockers.

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.210
Is something wrong?

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:45.450
Nope.

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:49.450
All we can do now is to get ready for the match.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.200
Let's stick this out!

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.120
Let's do this!

00:21:55.610 --> 00:21:57.930
I'm in!

00:21:57.930 --> 00:21:59.630
I'll do my best too!

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:04.920
Let's have fun...

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.920
and win!

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.060
Command!

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:12.930
Control!

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:15.190
Communication!

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:16.230
The C3 Club!

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:16.850
Yay!

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:20.070
Survival doesn't make the gunshots stop

00:22:20.070 --> 00:22:23.400
Carrying the flag I hear gunfire

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:28.530
Smile, 'cause isn't this fun?

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:30.620
Yay!

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:36.750
I blush when I make eye contact with my comrade,

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.580
but that's fine

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:41.710
Let's trust each other and laugh

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:42.710
Ready?

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:45.220
3, 2, 1, go! Go!

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:48.260
Take your comrade and get the flag!

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:51.970
Can't you feel your heart thump when you advance?

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:55.060
Let's hit them and laugh

00:22:55.060 --> 00:22:55.980
All right?

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:58.600
3, 2, 1, go! Go!

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.940
It can be hard, it can be vexing,

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.780
but when you overcome that

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:11.870
you'll smile like you never did before

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:13.580
Everyone, take up positions!

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:14.120
Okay!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:18.580
Survival doesn't make the gunshots stop

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:21.710
Carrying the flag I hear gunfire

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:25.800
Enjoy your youth, even if your tears are stolen

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:31.850
Telepathy, a step forward

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:34.890
Don't look down, look ahead

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:35.770
Sorry it took me so long to be enthusiastic about it!

00:23:39.730 --> 00:24:09.590
Preview

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:41.730
Oh no!

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:43.080
I forgot my sunscreen!

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:43.980
Want mine?

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:45.110
Thanks so much!

00:23:45.110 --> 00:23:46.730
What's your SPF, Kari?

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:49.030
I bought the wrong number, and now mine is too weak.

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:49.870
SPF?

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:51.400
SPF, not FPS.

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:54.880
No idea what you're talking about, but I never got sunburn with this.

00:23:54.880 --> 00:23:57.500
There's dirt in the tube!

00:23:57.500 --> 00:23:58.700
It's just sunscreen.

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:00.640
It looks cute in the tube.

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:01.320
I know, right?

00:24:01.320 --> 00:24:02.120
What?

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:09.590
Should the commander really be cold-blooded?

00:24:02.470 --> 00:24:03.370
Next episode.

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:04.710
Should the commander really be cold-blooded?

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:06.980
I'll go buy some over there.

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:08.320
Me too.
